How about a) all spells still obtained from spellbooks b) some of the spells 
would be permanent, some not and c) permanence (whattaheck is the right 
word???) might be gained via reading similar spellbooks many times e.g.
if you read three spellbooks of light, it'd give you a permanent spell of 
light (of course permanent genocide spell would need a lot more spellbooks of 
genocide). To make it a bit more difficult: forgetting spells should be
quite a usual thing to happen. Some monsters (magic attackers) might make 
you do it, some other scrolls than amnesia, quaffing (booze? :-), even some 
spellbooks (cursed ones?). Mana points should be reduced faster than now
to prevent generating spell'o'matic- wizards. There are many ways to prevent
spell-abusing, and I could find more but I just wanted to give a few 
suggestions.

